SORA 2 PROMPT — 15 SECONDS (MUSIC-DRIVEN / SPLIT-SCREEN EVOLUTION)

A fiery fox-hare hybrid made of living paint sprints through hell at impossible speed. The environment is an infernal wasteland of obsidian ground, lava fissures, collapsing gothic towers, firestorms, and demonic silhouettes.

Editing is driven entirely by the music rhythm. Every cut, transition, and camera move hits on the beat.

0–5s — TWO-PANEL SPLIT SCREEN:
– Left panel: ultra-wide rear tracking shot, the creature charging forward, paint and sparks ripping through the air
– Right panel: rapid rhythmic close-ups—claws striking ground, eye reflections, fire rushing past camera
Cuts snap aggressively on percussion hits. Panels subtly shake with bass impacts.

5–10s — THREE-PANEL SPLIT SCREEN:
– Center panel: frontal sprint toward camera through fire and smoke
– Side panels: demons lunging, lava eruptions, collapsing architecture
Panels slide, resize, and reconfigure on every musical accent. Motion blur intensifies.

10–15s — SHATTER TO FULL FRAME:
On a massive musical drop, the split-screen fractures violently into shards of fire and paint. The image slams into full frame.
– Slow-motion leap over a lava chasm
– Whip-pan into a demon attack narrowly missing the lens
– Overhead shot of the creature exploding through a swarm of enemies in a shockwave of color and fire

Music: relentless epic action score—heavy percussion, aggressive brass stabs, massive bass drops—cuts and transitions perfectly synchronized to rhythm.
Sound design: layered into the music—roaring flames, demonic screams, metallic impacts, explosive hits.

No dialogue. No voice over. No text.
Hyper-kinetic cinematography, painterly motion smear, high contrast cinematic lighting.
30fps, high definition, brutal momentum, nonstop energy.